          "kind": "text",
          "value": "📖 Passage / Context\nSuppose that a factory manufactures electronic gadgets every day. A quality control team tracks the number\nof defective gadgets found in daily production runs. Let 𝑋 be the number of defective gadgets produced on\nany given day. The mean and variance of 𝑋 are 50 and 81, respectively.\nBased on the above data, answer the given subquestions."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Using Chebyshev's inequality, find a lower bound on the probability that on a given day production will be\nbetween 30 and 70."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "9"
        }
      ],
      "marks": 3,
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Chebyshev gives P(|X−50|≥20)≤81/400. Consequently P(30≤X≤70)≥1−81/400=319/400, option C."
        }
